  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nNW flow behind an upper low passage continues to support lake-\nenhanced showers, primarily favoring the region downstream of a\nHuron-Erie fetch. For today and tonight, this will favor \nwestern PA and the WV high terrain with orographic influence, \nbut with a shortwave passage tonight, precipitation may shift \nsouthwest into eastern OH and the WV lowlands (as well as west \nPA) as 850mb flow remains more NNW through Sunday.\n\nMorning observations across the area have shown minimal snow\naccumulations below 2.5kft (i.e. PA/WV ridges), due mostly to\nsurface and 2m temperatures being to warm to support substantive\naccumulation and the top of the mixed layer only being around\n-11C. Some accumulations >0.5\" were observed in eastern Tucker \n County, which have already begun to melt.\n\nAs we head into the afternoon, only a meager warming is \nexpected, but nonetheless, all elevations below 3kft are \nexpected to see mostly rain showers apart from any of the most \nintense showers capable of producing graupel. For high terrain, \neven where snow is possible, accumulations are expected to be \nminimal during the daytime with radiative effects.\n\nOvernight, high terrain accumulations again become possible \nwith surface temperatures able to cool, with the Laurels \nshowing an 80% chance of non-zero accumulation, while the WV \nridges show a 90% chance. When talking about chances of >1\", \nthose same chances drop to <20%. Accumulation chances again drop\noff Sunday with diurnal influence before precipitation chances \ndiminish Sunday night.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nA pattern shift will be in-store for the next week with high\nconfidence in a return to drier and warmer conditions. All \nensemble clusters are practically in complete agreement for the \neast through next weekend, showing highs rebounding to the at \nleast the upper 50s by Thursday/Friday. Uncertainty trickles in \ninto next Saturday and beyond as to whether ridging and dry \nweather continues or the ridge amplitude flattens some with some\nlow rain chances.",
